# a2r emit basics (legacy `test/a2r` single-file goldens)

Oracles are the legacy `.expected.rs` files referenced in place — the
adapter path must be byte-identical to the legacy `test_a2r_with_base`
comparison. `module_name` mirrors the legacy stem derivation (metadata
parity; it does not affect emitted bytes).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/1"
  id: "trans.basics.func"
  tags: ["pilot", "a2r"]
  source: { file: "a2r/01_basics/003_func/func.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "emit", adapter: "a2r", action: "emit", tier: "trans-snapshot",
      options: { module_name: "func" },
      expect: { completion: "success", artifacts: [
        { path: "func.rs", file: "a2r/01_basics/003_func/func.expected.rs", compare: "bytes" } ] } }
  ]
}
```

